 "note": [
  "Scripture authority is the 1962 Amharic Bible (UBS; NT revised 2003). Its New Testament is on disk whole (ebible mirror gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/amh_amh; re-verified for this job: 27 NT books return 200, gen/isa/psa 404). The mirror carries no Old Testament, so OT quotations reuse the wording of an already-shipped Amharic work (source_file names it) and are otherwise self_rendered in the 1962 register.",
  "A `mined` row was re-measured against the finished text: an exact substring of at least 20 characters of the 1962 NT verse (or of the cited corpus file) inside that block. Shorter, re-personed or trimmed-and-adapted quotations are self_rendered, whatever the translator believed. The mirror files Romans 3:10's «ጻድቅ የለም አንድ ስንኳ» under 3:11 (1962 versification) and bridges 2 Cor 5:6-8, so 2 Cor 5:7 comes from the full edition's own wording.",
  "Family consistency: the epigraphs and every Spurgeon quotation reuse the shipped full edition (all-of-grace.am.json) wording; 2 Corinthians 5:7 follows that edition («በማየት ሳይሆን…») rather than the corpus's other form («በማየት አይደለም…»). The English quotes the ESV; per the Amharic teen editions the epigraphs cite book and verse with no version label. Pure allusions that quote no verse wording (Luke 15, Acts 9, Rev 3:20, Matt 9:12, John 3:8, Acts 16:26, Luke 22:60-61, Rom 8:15) are not listed."
